    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This thesis presents the development and evaluation of a prototype tool designed to personalize educational scenarios, thereby enhancing the effectiveness of scenario-based learning (SBL). Leveraging generative AI, the tool dynamically generates educational scenarios tailored to individual learners' interests, addressing gaps in personalizing SBL models to improve student engagement and information retention. The methodology includes tool development on AWS’s PartyRock platform, a two-phase user experience testing and evaluation process using quizzes and interviews. Findings from interviews suggest that personalized learning scenarios significantly increase user engagement, motivation, and agency. Notably, 95% of participants in the interviews anticipated better recall with personalized scenarios. However, quiz results indicated no significant difference in information retention between personalized and general scenarios, though they did reveal that participants tended to show more uncertainty with generalized scenarios and performed better on free-response questions for personalized scenarios. These outcomes imply that while personalization may enhance confidence, motivation, and engagement in learning experiences, it does not necessarily improve information retention. This study highlights the benefits of personalized learning in boosting engagement and motivation, yet emphasizes the need for additional research to enhance retention outcomes.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
